  'tutorial.submenus.title': 'Long menus are grouped', 'tutorial.submenus.text': 'Menus with many items are grouped into submenus by topic. Click an item with › on the right, or press →, and its submenu opens next to it (for example View › Switch view › Network diagram).',
  'tutorial.imageExport.title': 'The Gantt chart as an image', 'tutorial.imageExport.text': 'File › Import and export › Export as image: pick PNG, JPEG, WebP, BMP, TIFF or SVG, choose a transparent or white background, the table, the chart or both, and the scale and quality. A transparent image sits straight on top of documents and slides.',
  'tutorial.database.title': 'Keeping plans in a database', 'tutorial.database.text': 'In Settings › Database pick SQLite3, MariaDB, MySQL or PostgreSQL, enter the file or the server, port, database name and user, and press Test connection. From then on Save (Ctrl+S) writes both the file and the database, and File › Open from database brings plans back. The password is kept only if you turn on saving it.',
  'tutorial.reportExport.title': 'Exporting a report', 'tutorial.reportExport.text': 'The Export report button in the report header (or the Report menu) saves the current report as HTML, Markdown, Word (.docx) or PDF. Charts go in as pictures and the numbers as tables.',
